# Optional connection config for `test.sh` — copy to `.env` to point the test at ANY PostgreSQL with
# one value, without passing a variant folder or PG* env vars each time.
#   cp .env.example .env        # then uncomment ONE option below
# `.env` is gitignored. test.sh uses this only when you DON'T pass a TARGET arg or explicit PG* env.
# (Priority: PG* env > a connection-string arg / DATABASE_URL > THIS .env > a per-variant .env > defaults.)
# The dbname in a connection string is ignored — the test creates + drops its own throwaway database;
# the user needs CREATEDB (or superuser) rights and access to the `postgres` database.

# Option A — a single connection string (URI):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:yourpassword@127.0.0.1:5432/postgres

# Option B — individual libpq vars:
# PGHOST=127.0.0.1
# PGPORT=5432
# PGUSER=postgres
# PGPASSWORD=yourpassword
